## 11. COMMENTS, SELLER REPLIES, REPORTS, AND MODERATION

Audit the existing comment and reporting workflows.

### Comments

- Validate authenticated authorship.
- Prevent clients from forging usernames, roles, seller identities, or moderation flags.
- Enforce sensible content-length limits and field schemas.
- Prevent comment authors from changing moderation status or ownership.
- Validate seller replies against the seller who owns the advertised listing or campaign.
- Restrict edit/delete operations to authorized actors and permitted states.
- Apply server-side filtering or access control so hidden or removed comments cannot be retrieved through direct unauthorized queries.
- Preserve legitimate public seller replies and user interactions.

### Reporting

Implement reporting for both ads and individual comments.

Reports must include a validated target, reason, reporter identity, timestamp, status, and only the necessary contextual data.

Prevent duplicate abuse where appropriate, without preventing legitimate follow-up reports.

### Moderation

- Restrict moderation actions to authorized administrators.
- Add a report queue with priority based on credible fraud, scams, safety threats, prohibited products, and other documented severity criteria.
- Validate moderation decisions on the backend.
- Keep an audit trail of moderator actions.
- Support dismissal/no-action outcomes as well as content removal or other allowed actions.
- Notify relevant users where appropriate without revealing private reporter details unnecessarily.

The UI must reflect the server's authoritative moderation state.

